{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779046848,"nonce":"+AxMIAGJ0zMyTuupjz1RK9e3dko=","title":"Unified Chat/App Shell follow-up coordination","message":"## Problem\nThe unified Chat/History workspace and app-shell refactor have landed, but the remaining product work is now spread across older and newer issues. Several of those issues are durable backend/product follow-ups rather than polish: conversation identity, transport resume, model controls, project registry mapping, subagent nesting, sidebar reuse, and desktop-specific shell behavior.\n\nThis issue is the open coordination surface for that work. The goal is not to replace the specific implementation issues below; it is to keep them cross-referenced so future work does not regress the intended unified Chat/App Shell model.\n\n## Product direction\nMandible should treat conversations as one durable workspace, not separate live/history modes:\n- every conversation appears in the Chat sidebar, grouped by canonical project where available;\n- liveness is state on a conversation, not a separate section or tab;\n- the main pane shows the transcript/history and can continue the conversation when a supported transport exists;\n- transport/debug details stay secondary to the conversation;\n- the app shell uses a compact left rail plus view-specific secondary shelves/sidebars;\n- view shelves should be hideable/reopenable with consistent controls;\n- desktop-only affordances such as native titlebar placement should be tracked for the future wrapper rather than improvised in the web shell.\n\n## Coordinated follow-ups\nExisting issues that should be considered part of this follow-up set:\n- `8546c2f` — transcript rehydration, terminal fallback, Gemini, model picker.\n- `835e0bb` — resume live chat from history and Codex model presets.\n- `3da19be` — model/hyperparameter controls in the rich console/composer.\n- `3d85f43` — project registry and canonical name/path/source resolution for chat grouping.\n- `1b88786` — live subagent observation and nesting under parent conversations.\n- `48a58f7` — SDK-mediated subagent spawning and lifecycle control.\n- `7a95348` — shared sidebar/shelf component behavior across Auth, Issues, Chat, and other views.\n- `03a9f93` — unified chat history search CLI across providers.\n- `dfaf93c` — support multiple agent frameworks/transports.\n- `dffc52f` / `fdc0e8a` — desktop wrapper work where native shell/sidebar/titlebar behavior should eventually move.\n\nRecently merged implementation/context issues:\n- `10a4214` — unified Chat/History workspace with conversation sidebar.\n- `2b03ed3` — app rail/header restructure.\n- `67a12d9` — compact rail, grouped sidebar, composer fixes.\n- `466847f` — chat sidebar follow-up polish.\n\n## Coordination rules\n- Do not reintroduce separate Live and History sections as a primary information architecture.\n- Do not treat provider/session IDs or titles alone as durable conversation identity when exact conversation IDs exist or can be stored.\n- Do not solve project grouping through UI string cleanup only; route Claude/Codex/Gemini/session sources through the project registry.\n- Do not show subagents as independent top-level projects/conversations once parent-child metadata is available; nest them under the parent conversation or expose them through a focused activity surface.\n- Keep model/runtime controls near the composer or compact conversation actions, not as a third persistent sidebar.\n- Keep generated desktop-native placement decisions out of the web shell unless they also make sense in-browser.\n\n## Done means\nThe linked issues can be implemented independently without losing the unified product model: Chat remains one conversation-centered workspace, the app shell remains compact and consistent, provider-specific differences are behind adapters/registry data, and future desktop behavior has a clear place to land.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}